  "name": "Dumbbell-Weighted Supine Core Hold",
  "definition": "A bilateral weighted isometric performed supine with one round-head dumbbell held in both hands. From a bent-knee, dumbbell-at-shoulders setup, the athlete fixes the lower back to the floor, raises the head and shoulder-blade region, extends the arms beside the ears, straightens and raises both legs, and holds the long-lever shape. Gravity tends to extend the spine and hips; those are resisted tendencies rather than dynamic repetitions. This narrow contract does not include the unloaded Hollow Hold, medicine balls, plates, alternating limbs, rocks, presses, pullovers, or repeated leg lowering.",
