      "execution": {
        "startingPosition": "Lie on your back with both knees bent and hold the heads of one round-head dumbbell in both hands near your shoulders. Tilt your pelvis back and press your lower back into the floor.",
        "movement": "Raise your head and shoulder blades, extend the arms beside your ears, and straighten both legs to a height you can control without opening a gap beneath your lower back.",
        "endpoint": "Hold the long weighted shape for the set time with the dumbbell steady overhead.",
        "controlledJoints": "Keep the knees and elbows straight and keep the shoulders, spine, pelvis, and hips still.",
        "supportAndPosture": "Grip both dumbbell heads securely, record the dumbbell's total mass once, and keep the lower back in contact with the floor.",
        "disqualifyingCompensations": [
          "A gap opening beneath the lower back ends the strict hold.",
          "Bending the knees or elbows changes the reviewed long-lever fixture.",
